{"title":"Vega Logistics","sub":"Solar on the warehouse roof: buy the panels or buy the power?","type":"Investment / capacity","industry":"Energy","geo":"United States","diff":2,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"NPV · own vs lease · energy economics","prompt":"Vega runs a large distribution warehouse in Arizona. It can put solar panels on the roof for $1.5M, or let a solar developer install them for free and buy the power under a 25-year contract (a power purchase agreement, PPA). The CFO asks which is better, using Vega's 8% cost of capital.","clarify":[{"q":"Output?","a":"About 1,800 MWh a year for 25 years."},{"q":"How much would Vega use itself?","a":"About 70%; the rest would be exported to the grid when the warehouse is quiet."},{"q":"Prices?","a":"Vega pays $120 per MWh for grid power. Exported power earns $40 per MWh. Maintenance costs about $20k a year if Vega owns the panels."},{"q":"PPA?","a":"The developer would sell Vega the power it uses at $90 per MWh, and keep any exports."}],"structure":{"root":"Should Vega own the panels or sign a PPA?","branches":[{"head":"Owning","items":["Upfront cost","Yearly savings and export income","Maintenance","NPV over 25 years"]},{"head":"PPA","items":["Saving vs grid price","No upfront cost"]},{"head":"Other factors","items":["Use of capital","Risk of the roof or the business changing"]}]},"hypothesis":"Owning gives the full saving but ties up capital; a PPA gives a smaller saving with no investment. At an 8% cost of capital, the PPA could well win.","questions":[{"q":"What is owning worth, in NPV and payback?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Yearly benefit: 1,800 × (70% × $120 + 30% × $40) − $20k = <b>$152.8k</b>.</p> <p>25 years at 8% discount factor: 10.67. NPV = −$1,500k + $152.8k × 10.67 = <b>$131k</b>. Payback: 9.8 years.</p>","note":"Present value of $1 a year for 25 years at 8% = 10.67."},{"q":"What is the PPA worth?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"399.26pt\" height=\"176.64pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 399.26 176.64\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 176.64 L 399.26 176.64 L 399.26 0 L 0 0 L 0 176.64 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 46.1 139.04 L 392.06 139.04 L 392.06 11.528 L 46.1 11.528 L 46.1 139.04 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"ma99844d2ee\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#ma99844d2ee\" x=\"106.755325\" y=\"139.04\" style=\"fill: #4a5568; stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(75.372747 155.265) scale(0.09 -0.09)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-2c\" d=\"M 2266 -77 Q 1690 -77 1264 188 Q 838 454 604 969 Q 371 1485 371 2234 Q 371 2982 604 3497 Q 838 4013 1264 4278 Q 1690 4544 2266 4544 Q 2842 4544 3267 4278 Q 3693 4013 3926 3497 Q 4160 2982 4160 2234 Q 4160 1485 3926 969 Q 3693 454 3267 188 Q 2842 -77 2266 -77 z\nM 2266 403 Q 2656 403 2950 585 Q 3245 768 3414 1094 Q 3584 1421 3584 1862 L 3584 2605 Q 3584 3046 3414 3376 Q 3245 3706 2950 3885 Q 2656 4064 2266 4064 Q 1882 4064 1584 3885 Q 1286 3706 1116 3376 Q 947 3046 947 2605 L 947 1862 Q 947 1421 1116 1094 Q 1286 768 1584 585 Q 1882 403 2266 403 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-1a\" d=\"M 1082 0 L 198 3302 L 698 3302 L 1050 1875 L 1402 429 L 1414 429 L 1818 1875 L 2234 3302 L 2688 3302 L 3117 1875 L 3526 429 L 3539 429 L 3878 1875 L 4237 3302 L 4717 3302 L 3840 0 L 3206 0 L 2746 1587 L 2458 2592 L 2445 2592 L 2163 1587 L 1702 0 L 1082 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-11\" d=\"M 1056 0 L 544 0 L 544 3302 L 1056 3302 L 1056 2765 L 1082 2765 Q 1203 3046 1424 