are\"/></g><g id=\"text_10\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(99.555325 97.462178) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(211.88 28.02495) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\" d=\"M 1926 -77 Q 1466 -77 1130 131 Q 794 339 611 723 Q 429 1107 429 1638 Q 429 2138 573 2573 Q 717 3008 957 3373 Q 1197 3738 1475 4016 Q 1754 4294 2022 4467 L 2714 4467 Q 2240 4122 1897 3786 Q 1555 3450 1331 3059 Q 1107 2669 986 2150 L 1018 2138 Q 1126 2323 1270 2467 Q 1414 2611 1619 2694 Q 1824 2778 2093 2778 Q 2477 2778 2774 2611 Q 3072 2445 3241 2134 Q 3411 1824 3411 1402 Q 3411 966 3225 630 Q 3040 294 2707 108 Q 2374 -77 1926 -77 z\nM 1920 390 Q 2214 390 2422 499 Q 2630 608 2742 819 Q 2854 1030 2854 1331 L 2854 1382 Q 2854 1683 2742 1894 Q 2630 2106 2422 2214 Q 2214 2323 1920 2323 Q 1626 2323 1418 2214 Q 1210 2106 1098 1894 Q 986 1683 986 1382 L 986 1331 Q 986 1030 1098 819 Q 1210 608 1418 499 Q 1626 390 1920 390 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3c\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_12\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(324.204675 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pd2fb3de91e\"><rect x=\"46.1\" y=\"11.528\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · NPV at 8% ($k)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Vega saves $120 − $90 = $30 on each MWh it uses: 1,800 × 70% × $30 = $37.8k a year, with no investment.</p> <p>NPV: $37.8k × 10.67 = <b>$404k</b>, about 3× the NPV of owning.</p>"},{"q":"Owning only just pays. Why, and what could change that?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Thirty percent of the power is exported at $40, a third of the grid price, and Vega's 8% cost of capital is high for a 25-year asset. If Vega charged its electric forklifts in daytime and used 85% on site, owning would be worth $362k, still below the PPA.</p> <p>The developer can own panels more cheaply because its cost of capital is lower. Vega's capital is better spent on its core business.</p>"}],"reco":"Sign the PPA. Owning the panels has an NPV of only about $131k at Vega's 8% cost of capital, because 30% of the power is exported cheaply, while the PPA saves about $38k a year with no investment, an NPV of about $404k. Even using 85% of the power on site, owning stays behind. Negotiate the PPA price, a price-escalation cap and what happens if Vega leaves the building. Next step: get two more developer quotes.","great":["Values both options with the same discount rate and life","Values export and self-used power differently","Sees how cost of capital favours the PPA","Checks whether more self-use changes the answer"],"id":83,"slug":"vega-logistics"}